#: src/introduction.md:21
msgid "`just` is a handy way to save and run project-specific commands."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:23
msgid ""
"This readme is also available as a [book](https://just.systems/man/en/). The "
"book reflects the latest release, whereas the [readme on GitHub](https://"
"github.com/casey/just/blob/master/README.md) reflects latest master."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:28
msgid ""
"(中文文档在 [这里](https://github.com/casey/just/blob/master/README.中文."
"md), 快看过来!)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:31
msgid ""
"Commands, called recipes, are stored in a file called `justfile` with syntax "
"inspired by `make`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:34
msgid ""
"![screenshot](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/casey/just/master/etc/"
"screenshot.png)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:36
msgid "You can then run them with `just RECIPE`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:45
msgid "`just` has a ton of useful features, and many improvements over `make`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:47
msgid ""
"`just` is a command runner, not a build system, so it avoids much of "
"[`make`’s complexity and idiosyncrasies](what-are-the-idiosyncrasies-of-make-"
"that-just-avoids.html). No need for `.PHONY` recipes!"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:51
msgid ""
"Linux, macOS, Windows, and other reasonable unixes are supported with no "
"additional dependencies. (Although if your system doesn’t have an `sh`, "
"you’ll need to [choose a different shell](shell.html).)"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:55
msgid ""
"Errors are specific and informative, and syntax errors are reported along "
"with their source context."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:58
msgid ""
"Recipes can accept [command line arguments](recipe-parameters.html), "
"including [flags and options](recipe-parameters.html#recipe-flags-and-"
"options)."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:61
msgid ""
"`just` has a rich [expression language](expressions.html) and many built-in-"
"functions."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:64
msgid ""
"Wherever possible, errors are resolved statically. Unknown recipes and "
"circular dependencies are reported before anything runs."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:67
msgid ""
"`just` [loads `.env` files](dotenv-settings.html), making it easy to "
"populate environment variables."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:70
msgid ""
"Recipes can be [listed from the command line](listing-available-recipes."
"html)."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:72
msgid ""
"Command line completion scripts are [available for most popular shells]"
"(shell-completion-scripts.html)."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:75
msgid ""
"Recipes can be written in [arbitrary languages](shebang-recipes.html), like "
"Python or Node.js."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:78
msgid ""
"`just` can be invoked from any subdirectory, not just the directory that "
"contains the `justfile`."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:81
msgid ""
"`justfiles` can be organized into multiple files using [modules](modules."
"html) and [imports](imports.html)."
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:84
msgid "And [much more](https://just.systems/man/en/)!"
msgstr ""

#: src/introduction.md:86
msgid ""
"If you need help with `just`, please feel free to open an issue or ping me "
"on [Discord](https://discord.gg/ezYScXR). Feature requests and bug reports "
"are always welcome!"
msgstr ""
